Keep no login records where the C library has no utmp database.

The session helper writes utmp, wtmp and btmp records through
<utmp.h>/<utmpx.h> (setutxent, pututxline, updwtmp), which LikeOS's C
library does not have: it keeps no login records at all, and who is logged
in at the console is the kernel's to say.  The record keeping is compiled
only where the C library provides it.

